<span class="c"># evidence_nodes append provenance-tagged evidence</span>
for name, node in evidence_nodes.items():
  graph.add_node(name, node)
<span class="lit">graph.add_node("assess", assessor)</span>
graph.add_node("human_review", review_case)

graph.add_edge(START, "triage")
for name in evidence_nodes:
  graph.add_edge("triage", name)
graph.add_edge(list(evidence_nodes), "assess")
graph.add_conditional_edges("assess", route_case)
app = graph.compile(checkpointer=durable_store)</pre>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal">
          <h2>The assessment is an agent. The <em>route</em> is code.</h2>
          <div class="notes">
            <p class="note">Triage fans out; the join waits for required evidence.</p>
            <p class="note">Evidence is provenance-tagged and reducer-safe.</p>
            <p class="note">Conditional edges enforce policy routing.</p>
            <p class="note">Durable checkpoints make pause and resume explicit.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bottomline"><span>A graph is not automatically an agent; this node is</span><span class="folio">19 · 23</span></div>
    </section>

