    <!-- 22 · DECISION GUIDE ==================================== -->
    <section class="slide" data-slide="21" aria-label="Architecture decision guide">
      <div class="topline"><span class="mark"><i class="dot"></i>Decision guide</span><span>Choose by control flow, not fashion</span></div>
      <div class="main split">
        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">Start with the least freedom that creates value</p>
          <h2 class="wide" style="font-size:clamp(1.7rem,3.4vw,3.4rem)">Is the prebuilt loop enough?</h2>
          <div class="decision">
            <div class="branch"><q>Mostly predetermined path?</q><span class="answer">Normal code · fixed retrieval</span></div>
            <div class="branch"><q>Dynamic tool choice adds value?</q><span class="answer">LangChain agent</span></div>
            <div class="branch"><q>Must pause, persist, inspect, or enforce order?</q><span class="answer">Explicit LangGraph workflow</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal">
          <p class="eyebrow">One stack · different control</p>
          <div class="stack"><em>LangGraph runtime</em><br>└── LangChain create_agent<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;└── model ↔ tools loop<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;+ middleware</div>
          <p class="lede">The choice is rarely LangChain <em>or</em> LangGraph. It is whether you need to own the topology around the loop.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bottomline"><span>The abstractions compose</span><span class="folio">22 · 23</span></div>
    </section>

